<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.6.1: Evaluating Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02425</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.6.1: Evaluating Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>501242d9-8072-406c-ab1c-6c3ccc602302</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Each expression represents two numbers. Evaluate the expressions and find the <emphasis>two</emphasis> numbers.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="3367bcd2-5353-4c00-b027-056a5d3e866e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(1 \pm\sqrt{49}\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 8, -6</para><para>The correct answers are: 8, -6.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="3cf44a08-dd84-4e6f-9325-448021a03919" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\frac{8 \pm2}{5}\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para> Correct! 2, \(\frac65\)</para><para>The correct answers are:2, \(\frac65\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="588a324c-e455-438f-8480-1f3b842881cb" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\pm \; \sqrt{(-5)^2-4 \cdot 4 \cdot 1}\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3, -3</para><para>The correct answers are: 3, -3. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="9bcf7718-35b4-444e-b547-675c485075f3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\frac{-18 \pm \sqrt{36}}{2 \cdot3}\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -2, -4</para><para>The correct answers are: -2, -4. </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
